---
/** Slide 03 · Who builds software just changed — the vibe-coding shift. */
import InlineCitation from '@components/citations/InlineCitation.astro';
import { CITE } from './citations';
---

<section data-slot="03" data-variant="nf-p1" class="deck-section">
  <span class="deck-kicker">03 / 10</span>

  <div>
    <p class="deck-eyebrow mb-3">The shift</p>
    <h2 class="deck-h2">
      Vibe coding moved prototyping from the engineering backlog to
      <span class="deck-gradient">the domain expert's desk.</span>
    </h2>
  </div>

  <div class="deck-grid mt-2" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));">
    <div class="deck-card flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="deck-chip">UNTIL ~2025</span>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.15vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
        A domain insight became software only by hiring an engineering team —
        the expensive gate that kept the apprenticeship stack unbuilt.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="deck-card flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="deck-chip">NOW</span>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.15vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
        Agentic tools matured to where non-engineers ship working prototypes —
        Cursor, v0, Lovable, Bolt, Replit Agent, Claude
        Code.<InlineCitation {...CITE.get('b71a46')!} /><InlineCitation {...CITE.get('8cb194')!} /><InlineCitation {...CITE.get('e76b45')!} />
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="deck-card flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="deck-chip">STILL TRUE</span>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.15vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
        Engineers still own hardening, scale, and security — but they are no
        longer the gate on <em>prototyping</em>.<InlineCitation {...CITE.get('3675cf')!} />
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="deck-lede mt-2" style="max-width: 66ch;">
    The people who actually know what the apprenticeship stack needs —
    practitioners, industry-skills experts, adult educators — can now build
    the first version of the thing they understand.
  </p>
</section>
